{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 34, "timestamp": 1791020375, "title": "ForgeKeep: an agent opens a PR, a person approves it", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}}
[0.5, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Setting the stage: alice owns alice/app, bob reviews, alice-agent is an AI agent\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.328, "o", "  main is protected: 1 approval required; the agent's token is confined to alice/app\r\n"]
[8.53, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Agent → write_file: starts branch agent/answer with its first commit\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.168, "o", "  commit 38048a7c328c\r\n"]
[13.37, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Agent → create_pr\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[13.501, "o", "  #1 by alice-agent, acting for alice\r\n"]
[13.526, "o", "  CODEOWNERS requested: bob\r\n"]
[14.728, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.728, "o", "\u001b[1;36m▶ bob (code owner) leaves an inline comment\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.019, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Agent → list_review_comments\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.058, "o", "  The answer is 42.\r\n"]
[17.26, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Agent → read_file + write_file: fixes the code on its branch\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.991, "o", "  new head 0cd926ece0bf\r\n"]
[20.192, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ Agent → create_review_comment: answers in bob's thread\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.23, "o", "  replied to comment #1\r\n"]
[21.454, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ CI reports on the new head; agent → get_commit_status\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[21.508, "o", "  ci: success\r\n"]
[22.71, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ alice approves the agent's PR — and tries to merge\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.757, "o", "  merging into protected branch 'main' requires at least 1 approval(s), got 0 (1 more approval(s) do not count: an approval counts only from a person with write access who is neither the author nor, for a bot's pull request, the bot's owner)\r\n"]
[23.959, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ bob approves; the agent → merge_pr\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.034, "o", "  refused: 403 this token may not write to protected branch 'main'\r\n"]
[25.236, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m▶ alice merges\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[25.519, "o", "  #1 is merged; main: pub fn answer() -> i32 { 42 }\r\n"]
